WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.950
By bringing the entire Marvel Cinematic Universe
together to face off against a universe-threatening

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:08.980
bad guy, Marvel appears poised to make all
the money in the world when Avengers: Infinity

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:09.980
War hits theaters.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:14.350
The film looks huge, and everything we’ve
see so far has fans more than eager to see

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:18.340
more. But why exactly should this one knock
our socks off? From the ante-upping villain,

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.700
to fundamental changes in store for core Marvel
heroes, here's why we think Infinity War will

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.380
blow us all away.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:25.650
The next Darth Vader?

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.610
The entire MCU has been framed around the
idea that an insanely powerful villain by

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:34.170
the name of Thanos has been pulling the strings
behind most of the universe's problems. He’s

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:38.140
popped up in The Avengers and Guardians of
the Galaxy to cause trouble, sending lackeys

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.870
ahead of him in an effort to acquire the ultra-powerful
Infinity Stones.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:46.300
After years of setting him up, Infinity War
will finally place Thanos front and center,

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.819
and co-director Joe Russo has said that he’s
"hoping to make a Darth Vader for a new generation."

00:00:50.819 --> 00:00:54.930
With another Avengers sequel arriving in just
one year, he might remain a key player in

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:58.100
the MCU even after the dust settles from Infinity
War.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.799
Asgard go boom

00:00:59.799 --> 00:01:03.819
The first two installments of the Thor franchise
were arguably some of the weakest in Marvel's

00:01:03.819 --> 00:01:09.759
lineup, but all that changed in 2017. Under
director Taika Waititi, Thor: Ragnarok reinvigorated

00:01:09.759 --> 00:01:14.369
the series and added a sense of humor the
mainstream MCU never knew it was missing.

00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:15.940
“Shoo off, ghost!”

00:01:17.649 --> 00:01:21.580
It also featured some of the biggest character
growth yet for Chris Hemsworth's Thor. He

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:26.060
lost his hammer, his father, his eye, and
when Asgard was destroyed, his home.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:30.679
Despite the losses, Thor emerged a stronger
hero. Co-director Anthony Russo has said he

00:01:30.679 --> 00:01:35.380
feels Thor might be the most interesting character
heading into Infinity War after his "past

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.579
has been torn away from him." The one-eyed
Thor will have to overcome his losses in Ragnarok,

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:43.430
and find a new hammer, to take on the most
dangerous villain the heroes have ever faced.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:45.500
U Nomad, bro?

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:49.490
One of the biggest changes for the MCU over
the past few years is that when we pick up

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:53.810
the action in Infinity War, Captain America
might not even be Captain America anymore.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:58.289
The first glimpses we've gotten of Steve Rogers
show him sporting a beard and no shield — and

00:01:58.289 --> 00:02:02.700
in his most recent autograph signings, Cap
actor Chris Evans has been using the name

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.540
"Nomad" — a moniker Rogers took up in the
comics after becoming disillusioned with his

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:10.290
role as Captain America. There’s no word
on whether the big-screen version will follow

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:14.390
the same track, but Captain America: Civil
War pulled the Avengers apart — it'll be

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:17.710
interesting to see whether Infinity War can
bring them back together.

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:19.360
I am teenage Groot

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.250
There's no denying the role Groot has played
in the success of the Guardians' films, and

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:27.280
bringing him over to a mainline Avengers film
as a moody tree teen adds yet another bit

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.990
of geeky goodness to Infinity War. Motion
capture artist Terry Notary, who provided

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:35.970
the movements for Groot, said the character
will be "coming of age" in Infinity War, which

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:40.760
should make for one interesting subplot to
go along with all the world-ending stakes.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.120
Iron...Spider?

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:45.480
Fans got a brief peek at a new Spider-Man
suit at the end of Spider-Man: Homecoming,

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.940
and the trailers for Infinity War show Peter
Parker will definitely be taking advantage

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:54.070
of the upgrade when Thanos strikes. If you
pay attention to the LEGO toy tie-ins for

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:57.930
the film, though, we might just be seeing
another new design for Spidey: the Iron Spider

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:01.960
suit that Tony Stark made for Peter in the
comics. What better place to pull it out than

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.660
in Marvel's biggest movie ever?

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.390
Wakanda takes center stage

00:03:05.390 --> 00:03:10.110
Black Panther blew the roof off the box office
and made T’Challa an instant icon for superhero

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:13.780
fans. Luckily, they won’t have to wait to
see a lot more of the world of Wakanda.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:17.680
Every trailer and teaser for Infinity War
has made it abundantly clear that Black Panther

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.620
and Wakanda are going to be a huge factor.
They’re on full display, with plenty of

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:24.170
interactions between T’Challa and Steve
Rogers.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.720
“And get this man a shield.”

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.150
Giant-Size Marvel

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:33.120
As if it weren't already obvious, Infinity
War is poised to be Marvel's biggest movie

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.450
to date. It's bringing A-list stars and key
supporting players from every solo Marvel

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:41.720
franchise, loading the film with everyone
fans have come to know and love over a decade

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.690
of the MCU. But it doesn’t just combine
the Guardians of the Galaxy and the Avengers

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:49.160
into the same storyline. It brings them into
one single fight.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:53.180
Anthony Mackie, who plays Falcon, has said
it'll feature a scene with a mind-boggling

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:57.630
40 heroes onscreen at the same time, making
the massive brawl in Captain America; Civil

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:02.190
War look like a a tussle on the playground
by comparison. Marvel has flexed its blockbuster

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:06.550
muscle time and again over the last decade,
but Infinity War looks like it's really ready

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:10.180
to throw down the gauntlet — no pun intended.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:11.310
End of an era?

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:15.320
With Infinity War putting a cap on the first
ten years of the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:04:15.320 --> 00:04:19.130
it's hard not to start looking ahead at what
Disney's pending purchase of Fox could mean

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:23.530
for the future. If everything pans out, Marvel
may look to reacquire the rights to their

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.880
other two biggest teams: the Fantastic Four
and the X-Men.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:30.880
It stands to reason those characters will
eventually be folded into the MCU in the same

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.410
way that Spider-Man was brought in after Marvel
Studios cut a deal with Sony. Fans hoping

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:39.500
for a sneak peek in Infinity War will likely
be disappointed, though. Marvel Studios head

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:44.500
honcho Kevin Feige has made clear any potential
purchase will not impact the studio's current

00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:48.870
slate of productions lined up through 2019
— which include both Infinity War and its

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:53.530
untitled sequel. That slow roll is probably
a good thing, considering this movie is already

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:56.900
looking to juggle dozens and dozens of characters
as it stands.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:01.310
Thanks for watching! Click the Looper icon
to subscribe to our YouTube channel. Plus

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:03.260
check out all this cool stuff we know you'll
love, too!

